{Presiding: Committee Chair; Member for Maafushi constituency Hussain Riza Adam}

Statement by the Chair:

Assalaamu alaikum. I welcome the participants of the 21st meeting of the People's Majlis Committee on Independent Institutions. Taking part in this meeting are the Honourable Member for West Henveyru constituency Ali Ibrahim, the Honourable Member for Kolamaafushi constituency Ibrahim Didi, the Honourable Member for Dhidhdhoo constituency Abdul Latheef Mohamed and the Honourable Member for South Fuvahmulah constituency Ibrahim Hussain. First in today's meeting is the National Integrity Commission. Then second, as part of reviewing the 2025 annual reports of the Anti-Corruption Commission, the presentation of those institutions' annual reports. Then after the presentations, if anyone has any question regarding the work those institutions are carrying out or regarding the presentation submitted, there will be an opportunity to put questions to those parties. At this point I would like to say this to the committee members and to the institution's officials. So, the Integrity Commission first. The Honourable Member for Baarah constituency Ibrahim Shujau has joined our meeting. (After a short pause) Assalaamu alaikum. Yes! We have asked the members of the National Integrity Commission to submit to this committee a summary presentation of the report on how the National Integrity Commission operated in the past year. Then after the submission, if our members have something further to clarify, or have a question to ask, that part can proceed. I welcome all participants of the meeting. Taking part in this meeting are the President of the Commission, Shuaib Abdul Rahman. The Vice President of the Commission, Fathimath Shareef. Commission member, Mariyam Insha Faisal. Commission member, Shifaz Ali. Commission member, Ali Mohamed Manik. Secretary General, Nafha Hussain and Director, Fathimath Nizna. We are running a little later than the time we expected. We expected to start at 11 o'clock. However, after we came here, while we were ready to start, a vote had to be taken, and all of us members had to go to complete that vote. I think this started around the time it should have finished. For that I sincerely apologise to everyone. So, shall we proceed? Then every
